</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 4:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s a thought, back in the Day when Rader thought he ws a big serial killer, and wanted everone to know it, He was copying other killers MO and Trying to Be even more Famous then Zodiac or Jack the Ripper, So why did he all of a sudden disappear from all that fame and glory? What if another Killer, someone Rader had looked up to and was seeking advice from, got a little upset that Rader was stealing his thunder, and Told Rader if you don&#39;t knock it off I will make you one of My victims. What do you all think? Sense we know he was communicating with other killer&#39;s<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11403-->
<!--Post: 11410--><!--Time: 1110677272-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11410"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 5:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why do you believe he was communicating with other killers. Your whole post is extremly far-fetched. I think your are making the mistake of trying to add mystery to something that is already solved. There are plenty of things to discuss about the BTK case, your actual idea for the thread is a great area of discussion, however I think your over reaching. He stopped communicating for much more simple reasons. He was frustrated it wasn&#39;t garnering him the exposure he hoped to recieved.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
