</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 3:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read a news artical from outside the Wichita area &#40;which is the best place to find NEW information since everyone around here is under a gag &#34;threat&#34;&#41;which said that authorities feel that his dog catcher job gave him enough of a feeling of authority to keep his killing in his pants. <BR> <BR>Personally, I doubt that would do it, but if it didn&#39;t he at least got smart enough to change his M.O..<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11437-->
<!--Post: 11442--><!--Time: 1110730965-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11442"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 8:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok Johno, when DTDC did stop communicating with LE &#40;whatever year that was&#41; as those of us who have kids know how demanding they can be with extra curricular activites and such &#40;boy scouts etc.&#41; DTDC, grew a conscience through the reality of his own children and began to fight the monster within him. It was fruitless because the monster obviously won. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11442-->
<!--Post: 11449--><!--Time: 1110753900-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11449"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 2:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lola go to messages to btk read all the messages from part 3 and 4 there is to much to explain in this little thread, if you look you will see what I mean. And Rocky I agree with you, my problem is that Rader is not like us, he didn&#39;t care about people, so how could a sociopath just all of a sudden control the urges. Why couldn&#39;t he do that any other time. Unless in his obsession he was trying to follow Zodiac to a Tee because it took Z something like 27 years I think to write again. Could he really have been that much in control of what he did all those years? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11449-->
<!--Post: 11465--><!--Time: 1110770305-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11465"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 7:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Again, he didn&#39;t stop communicating with LE because he never communicated with them in the first place.  <BR>The 911 call reporting the Nancy Fox murder in 1977 was the only time he ever directly contacted anyone associated with law inforcement prior to his one letter to Wichita police in 2004. <BR>All other communications were to newspapers, television stations and to Anna Williams and possibly the widow of Phillip Fager. <BR>The only other known BTK communication was the first one in 1974 to Wichita Eagle TIPS hotline operator Don Granger. <BR>Many of these communications of course had instructions for and messages to LE but only the December 1977 Fox call and the June 2004 Wichita police letter were ever in direct contact with LE. <BR>I see no evidence of him ever fighting this so called &#39;monster.&#39; <BR>He got married and had a family because that was something that someone from his generation was supposed to do. It was expected of him. He never showed any regard to his family when it came to being BTK. <BR>He sent the Oh Anna poem to Anna Williams on the day of his daughters first birthday. <BR>Rocky, he killed your nieghbor and your mother&#39;s friend Marine Hedge on his wife&#39;s birthday. <BR>The monster story is his way of manipulation. There was no monster for him to fight. the monster was him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11465-->
<!--Post: 11476--><!--Time: 1110779167-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11476"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 9:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok Johno, I&#39;m trying to substantiate competency and knowing right from wrong within his communications. By contacting the LE, wouldn&#39;t that be an admission of &#34;hey I did something wrong and that&#39;s why I&#39;m calling you or writing you to tell you about it.&#34; If so, then your right there was no monster.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11476-->
<!--Post: 11495--><!--Time: 1110784176-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11495"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 11:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yeah you&#39;r e right it&#39;s like a kid going &#34;nah, nah, nah, nah, you can&#39;t catch me.&#34; <BR>Doing something you know is wrong and then laughing about it. <BR>That&#39;s no sign of a guy fighting a monster. <BR>Jeffery Dahmer, killing and telling no one his horrible secret side. There&#39;s a guy with a monster. <BR>Dennis Rader does horrible things and toys with his victims and then toys with media, police, community etc.. he&#39;s the monster.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11495-->
<!--Post: 11537--><!--Time: 1110895568-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11537"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 6:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very good point Johno, In my sorting of this mess I had overlooked the obvious, I am still glad I started the thread becuase it is bringing out the other points, Was Dennis in control of his actions, I agree that he was.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11537-->
<!--Post: 11552--><!--Time: 1110904894-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11552"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 8:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think Bmodule hit the nail on the head. To expand on the information he referred to, IMHO Rader didn&#39;t need the same frequency or intensity of serial killing because he was allowed to vent that need for control through his work and personal life. How many of us have read about serial killers who murder because they don&#39;t have a lot of control in their personal lives, work, etc.? <BR> <BR>Rader is an exception. He had an everday opportunity to bully, threaten and terrify the people around him. Hence, his need to kill was lessened. Does that mean he stopped? Hell, no, but the frequency, violence and ritualism were probably mitigated. I believe his need to get attention about them was lessened too. That explains the gap in communications. Then, recently he loses control over the people closest to him &#40;they move away, become ill, etc.&#41; and he feels the need to get control over something and the communications start again.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11552-->
<!--Post: 11558--><!--Time: 1110907422-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11558"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 9:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with ivy leaguer he stopped to avoid apprehension. Yes. However, I believe his ego would not have allowed him to stop if back in the early days he got the press exposure he wanted so much.  If his case got as much media as say the son of sam murders he would have kept communicating. Thats what got him caught this time around. I don&#39;t buy the &#34;he wanted it to end&#34; stuff. He wanted it to go on as long as it could. After all the years he played second fiddle in the world of serial killers, he was getting his day as the #1 story. Its a terrible way to look at it I know but I think its closer to the truth at his motivation for the past years communications. I think he started with the first letter back in response to the newspaper article and once he got those national headlines he couldn&#39;t stop.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11558-->
<!--Post: 11600--><!--Time: 1110933513-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11600"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 4:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I also noticed this 01/15/74 Otero murders <BR>1/21/74 bruce douglas <BR>4/4 Kathern Bright  And in october the letter was found in the Engineering book <BR>Zodiac <BR>1974 the Zodiac Resurfaced 1st letter sent 1/29 <BR>2nd letter 2/14/74 <BR>3rd letter 5/8/74 <BR>last letter 6/8/74 <BR>do you think they were talking oh yeah in the Z files he was suppose to be a cop or Engineer Why would Z come back, or Rader kill a family, we may never know<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11600-->
<!--Post: 11621--><!--Time: 1110951424-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11621"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 9:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E, <BR> <BR>IMO the Zodiac is dead. IMO if the Zodiac were still alive and let&#39;s say for the sake of my point he was also BTK.  .  . the Zodiac would NEVER EVER have sent a computer disk to police. The Zodiac would have studied computer technology, email communications and he would have known NOT to have sent in that disk.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Rader was never as smart as the Zodiac.  .  .  imo<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11621-->
<!--Post: 11641--><!--Time: 1110959495-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11641"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 11:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have a hard time believing that Rader did all of the BTK stuff by himself, let alone Zodiak&#39;s job too...and on top of that, keep the stray dogs under control in smallville.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11641-->
<!--Post: 11665--><!--Time: 1111017350-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11665"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 3:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As Ivy Leaguer and Scbenson2001 wrote, I believe Rader stopped communication with the <i>media</i> to lessen his chance of capture. After all, if Rader didn&#39;t restart his communications a year ago, he&#39;d still be free. <BR> <BR>The one powerful similarity between Zodiac and Rader were that they communicated with the press. Other than that, Zodiac and BTK are quite dissimilar in most respects. Fatidic dates common to Z and Rader start to give me a headache after a while. Maybe some are significant, and there&#39;s no question Rader was influenced to a degree, as were others, by Zodiac. <BR> <BR>EAR/ONS, other than not writing letters &#40;he did phone one person&#41; is much closer to Rader than was Zodiac in terms of the actual crimes -- the home invasions and murder, in my opinion, are something Zodiac would not have dreamed of in 1968 or 1969, the two years in which all definite Zodiac victims were murdered. Zodiac required a comparatively enormous outdoor setting in very remote areas, excepting Stine, while Rader&#39;s definite crimes don&#39;t cover nearly as much real estate as Z and were committed in neighborhoods. <BR> <BR>But the communication is signal and without it, Rader wouldn&#39;t have been apprehended. Unfortunately, Zodiac&#39;s communiques didn&#39;t result in his capture.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11665-->
<!--Post: 11669--><!--Time: 1111018272-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11669"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 4:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, <BR> <BR>Powerful as it may seem, the Zodiac communicated on a completely different level than BTK. The Zodiac was a trained and talented code master.  <BR> <BR>One of his coded messages could not be solved by &#34;expert&#34; military, FBI, &amp; DOJ code breakers. It was a married couple that broke this code.  <BR> <BR>On the other hand BTK sends in Sunday newspaper quality word scrambles with very little expertise needed.  <BR> <BR>I agree BTK was influenced and attempted to copy the Zodiac but BTK was in NO way as intelligent as the Zodiac. <BR> <BR>The Zodiac killed his victims in remote &#34;unincorporated&#34; areas where police agency responsibilities were often unclear leading to confusion during intial investigative process. <BR> <BR>I guarantee that if the Zodiac were still alive, he is long gone, he would have sent a message after all the publicity BTK is getting.  <BR> <BR>I also guarantee that the Zodiac would have studied computer communications &amp; technology and he would NEVER have made the bungling mistake of sending the police a computer disc !<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11669-->
<!--Post: 11701--><!--Time: 1111034482-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11701"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 8:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tac - how is it that you could guarantee anything? Especially after DTDC was the master of deceit? How do you know that Zodiac isn&#39;t still alive? You talk as though it&#39;s all past tense.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11701-->
<!--Post: 11729--><!--Time: 1111084538-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11729"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 17, 2005 - 10:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes you are right Zodiac is very well educated and Rader was a copycat, just wanted to see what type of response I would get. You are all on the ball today lol Thanks E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11729-->
<!--Post: 11747--><!--Time: 1111109291-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11747"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 17, 2005 - 5:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, <BR> <BR>&#34;DTDC WAS the master of deceit&#34; The word was is past tense. IMO it is past tense. A monsterous ego such as the Zodiac would never be able to tolerate the type of press generated by BTK without sending his opinion.  .  . <BR> <BR>It is speculation that killers, rapist, or child molesters can be &#34;corrected&#34; or cured. It has also been some psychologist speculation that  monsters such as the Zodiac or BTK sometimes &#34;burn out&#34; and stop killing as they get older.  .  .  <BR> <BR>He might have stopped killing but the Zodiac would not have stopped communicating.  .  .  I guarantee it. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11747-->
<!--Post: 11790--><!--Time: 1111177352-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11790"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lizzie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lizzie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 12:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think he stopped communicating, in part, because of what he learned at WSU about admin. of justice. Didn&#39;t he graduate in 1979? He would have also been trying to get into the WPD then. Maybe he learned new investigative techniques, etc. I think he changed his MO because of what he learned there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11790-->
<!--Post: 11804--><!--Time: 1111194781-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11804"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 5:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The reason he stopped probably involved a lot of individual factors such as DNA technology, emergence of computer networks &amp; internet, possibly even microbiology. All in all it boils down to there were more ways to trace him and he had to make a choice between killing and taunting the cops. <BR> <BR>He changed his M.O. in his later killings, which would suggest that he wanted to keep killing but didn&#39;t want the murders connected to him. <BR> <BR>Apparently he realized that he wasn&#39;t as smart as he thought, and to feed them information would trip him up. <BR> <BR>Then, apparently, he forgot. nyuk, nyuk, nyuk. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11804-->
